// CONFORMANCE-CASE
// spec: 22-surface-syntax
// facility: spec/22 §3 for's body is a block (D-0035)
// kind: negative
// expect: parse-error
//
// In C, `for (…);` is an empty loop, and the block after it runs
// once, unconditionally: a mistake that compiles. Here the body is
// always a block, so the `;` is a syntax error that says so.

fn main()
{
    i32 i = 0;
    for (i32 i = 0; i < 3; i += 1);
    {
        i += 1;
    }
}
